# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   See https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv/header-python-version
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if used with a pyproject.toml, the lock file should be ignored.
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipenv, poetry.lock should generally be tracked unless it's a library.
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipenv, pdm.lock should generally be tracked unless it's a library.
#.pdm-python.path
#.pdm-build/

# PEP 582; dependency directory created by pipflow
